Subject: Tag the QR-code action test with the qrcode group

Matches Debian's own precedent (see the dropped mark-flaky-tests-as-such.patch
in salsa's history, which tagged this same test for the same reason before
upstream's phpunit-11 restructure renamed it): QrcodeTest::test_run's own
check_support() call determines at runtime whether BaconQrCode is usable and
calls markTestSkipped() if not, rather than failing outright - the test file
itself expects this to be a legitimate, environment-dependent skip. But
`--fail-on-skipped` (see debian/rules) turns any skip into a build failure
unless it's in an excluded group, and unlike Debian's own control file (which
only drops php-bacon-qr-code, and so only excludes this group, on
architectures lacking it), this build's environment doesn't make
BaconQrCode's classes available even on amd64. Excluding the group
unconditionally in debian/rules (rather than only for 32-bit archs) covers
that too.

Forwarded: not-needed
---
